kmsro, dril, loader: sgx as a render-only GPU

kmsro pairs a KMS-only display device with the SGX under powervr_sgx: a
scanout buffer is a dumb buffer of the display device, imported into the
GPU.

powervr_sgx is a PCI device on the CE5300 (the SGX is its own PCI function)
and an auxiliary device of gma500's PCI function on Cedarview:
- a platform display device such as simpledrm on a boot framebuffer has to
  find its render node off the platform bus: render nodes of PCI devices are
  taken when their driver is powervr_sgx;
- a display device on another bus (gma500, PCI) gets the render node of a
  child of its own device, when that node's driver is in kmsro's list.
  libdrm's device list leaves out the auxiliary bus, so the loader finds the
  child through /sys/class/drm (loader_find_child_render_node, with a unit
  test on fake sysfs trees).

EGL gives a display an EGLDevice from libdrm's device list. A display
device whose render node libdrm can't describe (the auxiliary-bus SGX) goes
with the software device's entry, as a primary-node-only device does;
without it eglInitialize fails on gbm and X11 (Xorg's glamor on Cedarview).

An X server's GLX (AIGLX) loads <display driver>_dri.so: dril stubs for
simpledrm, gma500 and sgx.

